Regarding the issue of violating double blindness, as a reviewer, my responsibility is merely to identify and point it out. The decision-making of desk rejection or not rests with the Area Chair; 

Regarding the relevant dataset, I know that Neurips 2022 has a non-public dataset that can be used to test BBQ performance, but I don't know how to obtain it. Perhaps the authors could try to fetch such dataset.

As for the overall evaluation of this paper, since I am not an expert in this (theoretical) field, it is difficult for me to assess its specific theoretical value. However, I see broad application prospects in it. Ignoring the double blindness issue, I would give it a 6/10.
